@startuml usecases-access
' page: landscape
!include _usecase-style.puml
title Access use cases (draft)

' Shows who starts which Access use case, and where Keycloak takes part.
' Not drawn: the rules each use case applies, and the other contexts (Projects, Evaluations).
' Evolved from MK3 UC-A1 to UC-A7. MK3 UC-A7 is UC-A4 here (see the source specs).
' Green = built. Grey = not built (UC-A7 is Release 2).


actor "Person\n(not signed in)" as Visitor #1565C0
actor "Signed-in\nperson" as Member #1565C0
actor "Administrator" as Admin #E65100
actor "Keycloak" as KC #6B7280

rectangle "Access (BC-ACCESS)" #F2F6FC {
  usecase "UC-A1\nSign in" as UCA1 COLOR_BUILT
  usecase "UC-A3\nRegister and wait\nfor approval" as UCA3 COLOR_BUILT
  usecase "UC-A7\nSign in through\ncompany SSO" as UCA7 COLOR_TODO
  usecase "UC-A2\nSign out" as UCA2 COLOR_BUILT
  usecase "UC-A5\nView my name\nand role" as UCA5 COLOR_BUILT
  usecase "UC-A6\nKeep the session\nalive" as UCA6 COLOR_BUILT
  usecase "UC-A4\nApprove, deactivate, reinstate,\npromote and demote an account" as UCA4 COLOR_BUILT
}

UCA1 -[hidden]right-> UCA3
UCA3 -[hidden]right-> UCA7
UCA2 -[hidden]right-> UCA5
UCA5 -[hidden]right-> UCA6
UCA1 -[hidden]down-> UCA2
UCA6 -[hidden]right-> UCA4
Visitor --> UCA1
Visitor --> UCA3
Visitor --> UCA7
Member --> UCA2
Member --> UCA5
Admin --> UCA4

' UC-A6 is started by the web server on the person's behalf, so it is drawn as included.
UCA5 .> UCA6 : <<include>>
UCA4 .> UCA6 : <<include>>

' Keycloak takes part in these (it holds the login, the session and the enabled flag).
UCA1 -- KC
UCA3 -- KC
UCA7 -- KC
UCA2 -- KC
UCA6 -- KC
UCA4 -- KC

legend bottom right
  Green: built. Grey: not built.
  Keycloak is a secondary actor: it proves who the person is.
  Playground's account decides what the person may do.
endlegend
@enduml
